{
  // Typecheck gate for `tests/`, which the main tsconfig deliberately omits
  // (`include: ["src/**/*.ts"]`) and which `tsx` never checks — it strips types
  // and runs. In community-agent that gap hid a whole class of test bug: an
  // injected-deps object that omits a field silently falls through to the REAL
  // repository function, so a "unit" test quietly queries live Postgres, and
  // because `node:test` runs test FILES in parallel those stray reads land on
  // tables other files are counting. The same trap will exist here the moment
  // the runtime and its DB-backed tests are extracted, so the ratchet is set up
  // now, while the list is short enough to be complete.
  //
  // This is an INCREMENTAL RATCHET, not a big-bang switch: `include` lists only
  // test files that are type-clean today. Adding a file is the unit of progress
  // — bring it to zero errors, then list it here and it can never regress.
  // Never delete an entry to turn a red build green.
  //
  // Listed alphabetically, one per line, so two PRs adding different files land
  // in different hunks and merge cleanly (same reasoning as
  // tests/security-floor.json's per-file entries).
  //
  // The list is currently exhaustive — every test file in the repo is clean.
  // It stops being exhaustive the first time the extraction pass lands a test
  // file with a pre-existing error; that is expected and is what the ratchet is
  // for. (`include` is never left literally empty: tsc errors with "No inputs
  // were found" and the gate would fail for a reason that has nothing to do
  // with test types.)
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    // tests/ sits outside src/, so the shared rootDir has to widen for this
    // project. noEmit means nothing is written regardless.
    "rootDir": "."
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "tests/moduleApi.test.ts"]
}
